WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.049
I finished high school at sixteen after illness

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:07.197
repeatedly interrupted the year. My examination results

00:00:07.197 --> 00:00:10.796
cost me the medical-school path I had expected.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.967
I finished school at sixteen. The disease had already

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.094
interrupted my last year, and my examination results

00:00:23.094 --> 00:00:26.220
closed the medical school path I had expected.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.827
During severe attacks I could not always keep down even

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:40.891
water. Laboratory eosinophil counts became numbers I

00:00:40.891 --> 00:00:43.517
learned to anticipate from the pain.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.471
One week before a trip to the United States, an actual

00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:55.761
flare led to an endoscopy and a course of

00:00:55.761 --> 00:00:57.954
glucocorticoids. It was not preventive treatment.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.557
Clinical uncertainty turned into an accumulation of

00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:10.665
medications, tests, missed days and attempts to

00:01:10.665 --> 00:01:13.772
understand what my own body was doing.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.719
Years later I could sometimes anticipate an eosinophil

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:25.805
count from the severity of a flare, but no number

00:01:25.805 --> 00:01:27.439
captured vomiting even water.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.675
I learned to investigate cells and materials while

00:01:36.675 --> 00:01:39.901
living with a disease whose symptoms could overwhelm

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.513
even an ordinary day.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.086
The essay is a first-person account of what happened,

00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:54.317
not a dramatic reenactment of a medical record.
